+  <request name="set_view_source" since="4">
+    <description summary="select the same native source rectangle in both views">
+      Select a rectangle independently within each view of side_by_side_full
+      content. Coordinates are native buffer pixels after the buffer transform,
+      relative to the top left of each half of the viewport source rectangle.
+      The viewport destination remains the logical size of one drawing area.
+      No new packing or view-order value is introduced.
+
+      The rectangle is double buffered with wl_surface.commit. Initially it is
+      unset. Set all four values to -1 to unset it. Otherwise x and y must be
+      nonnegative and width and height strictly positive. The rectangle must
+      fit inside each view when a buffer is committed; otherwise bad_source is
+      raised. With no viewport destination, the rectangle's size divided by
+      buffer scale gives the surface size. Fractional edges are retained.
+
+      Setting content to none or destroying the declaration also unsets the
+      rectangle. This request on a destroyed wl_surface raises no_surface.
+      Existing clients which do not set a view source keep their behavior.
+    </description>
+    <arg name="x" type="fixed"/>
+    <arg name="y" type="fixed"/>
+    <arg name="width" type="fixed"/>
+    <arg name="height" type="fixed"/>
+  </request>
 </interface>
 
